<title>GERMANY: Krupp-annual steel merger synergies 550 mln dmk.</title>
<headline>Krupp-annual steel merger synergies 550 mln dmk.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Krupp AG chief executive Gerhard Cromme said on Friday he expected synergies from the German firm's joint steel venture with Thyssen AG of 550 million marks a year from 2001.</p>
<p>Cromme made the forecast at a news conference in Essen, at which he said he was satisfied with the merger agreement reached with Thyssen this week, at the expense of Krupp's original hostile takeover bid for its steel industry rival.</p>
<p>The joint venture, which takes effect April 1, will be called Thyssen Krupp Stahl and will be Europe's biggest steel company with sales of 11 billion marks and output of 15 million tonnes a year.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
